Package: SwitchEconometrics
Type: Package
Title: Unified Estimation of Endogenous Regime-Dependent Economic Systems
Version: 1.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ibrahim", "Niankara", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "Ibrahim.niankara@aau.ac.ae"),
    person("BRASS Digital Lab", role = "fnd",
           comment = "LLC registered in Burkina Faso, RCCM BF-OUA-01-2026-B13-02466; https://brassbe1982-bdlweb.share.connect.posit.cloud/"))
Description: Estimation and inference for the classical binary endogenous
    switching regression model (Heckman (1979) <doi:10.2307/1912352>;
    Lokshin and Sajaia (2004) <doi:10.1177/1536867X0400400306>), the sample
    selection model and the endogenous treatment model with a shift (Heckman
    (1978) <doi:10.2307/1909757>), and switching regression with
    multinomial-logit selection among any number of regimes (Lee (1983)
    <doi:10.2307/1912003>; Dubin and McFadden (1984) <doi:10.2307/1911493>;
    Bourguignon, Fournier and Gurgand (2007)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1467-6419.2007.00503.x>), built on a
    general model of regime selection and regime-specific outcomes that is
    designed to extend to multinomial switching, copula dependence and
    panel data. Provides full-information maximum
    likelihood with an analytic gradient and Hessian, two-step estimation
    with corrected covariances, Hessian, sandwich and cluster-robust
    standard errors, bootstrap, likelihood-ratio and Wald tests,
    identification diagnostics, treatment effects on the treated and
    untreated with their heterogeneity (Di Falco, Veronesi and Yesuf (2011)
    <doi:10.1093/ajae/aar006>), counterfactual and policy scenarios, and
    simulation.
